artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $V$ be a finite-dimensional complex vector space and let $S^d V$ denote the space of homogeneous polynomials of degree $d$ on $V^*$ (equivalently, symmetric tensors of order $d$ over $V$). An algebraic branching program (ABP) of width $r$ computing a homogeneous polynomial $f \in S^d V$ is a directed acyclic graph with a source $s$ and a sink $t$, whose vertices are partitioned into $d+1$ ordered layers, such that:
- the source $s$ is the unique vertex in the first layer and the sink $t$ is the unique vertex in the last layer;
- every other layer contains at most $r$ vertices;
- each edge goes from a vertex in layer $i$ to a vertex in layer $i+1$ and is labeled by a linear form in $V$;
- $f$ equals the sum, over all directed paths from $s$ to $t$, of the products of the labels along the path.

Define
$$\mathrm{IMM}_{r,V} \;:=\; \overline{\{[f] \in \mathbb{P}(S^d V) : f \text{ is computable by an ABP of width at most } r\}} \;\subseteq\; \mathbb{P}(S^d V),$$
the Zariski closure of the projective set of homogeneous polynomials of degree $d$ admitting an ABP of width $\le r$.

Problem. For small values of $r$ and small values of $\dim V$, determine explicit defining polynomial equations (i.e., generators of the homogeneous ideal, or at least set-theoretic defining equations) of the projective variety $\mathrm{IMM}_{r,V} \subseteq \mathbb{P}(S^d V)$.

